-- ============================================================================
-- crude ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Crude Assay & Blending, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE ASSAY AND THE BLEND. API is a hyperbola in
-- specific gravity and is never averaged on volume; specific gravity blends on
-- volume; sulfur, TAN, nitrogen and the metals blend on mass, from mass shares
-- the engine forms once; viscosity blends through the Refutas index; a TBP
-- curve answers only between its measured points and where it says so itself,
-- and a cut is a difference of two readings; the colloidal instability index
-- screens a blend, and the gravity rule of thumb can raise a flag and never
-- clear one.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. A blank is absent. A property blends only
-- when every crude carries it, and the engine names the crude that does not.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The wrong basis gives a plausible number.
-- API averaged on volume, sulfur on volume and SARA on volume each land close
-- to the right figure and are each wrong, and the digest prints them side by
-- side.
--
-- HELD, taught as a limit and never graded: the Refutas index blended on mass
-- (C12). Every figure is invented and illustrative. The capstone grades six
-- four-decimal engine figures at a tolerance of 5e-5.
-- ============================================================================

values ('crude', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-an-assay-carries","title":"What an Assay Carries","lesson_keys":["l01-four-questions-an-assay-answers","l02-api-gravity-is-a-hyperbola","l03-the-crude-library","l04-two-modules-and-a-kernel"]},{"key":"m02-blending-on-the-right-basis","title":"Blending on the Right Basis","lesson_keys":["l01-density-blends-on-volume","l02-api-through-specific-gravity","l03-volume-shares-become-mass-shares","l04-sulfur-blends-on-mass","l05-a-blank-is-not-a-zero"]},{"key":"m03-viscosity-through-an-index","title":"Viscosity Through an Index","lesson_keys":["l01-why-viscosity-needs-an-index","l02-the-refutas-index","l03-the-index-blends-on-mass","l04-where-the-index-has-no-answer"]},{"key":"m04-the-curve-and-its-cuts","title":"The Curve and Its Cuts","lesson_keys":["l01-a-tbp-curve-is-cumulative","l02-between-the-measured-points","l03-outside-the-measured-points","l04-a-cut-is-a-difference","l05-a-cut-set-that-closes"]},{"key":"m05-will-the-blend-stay-stable","title":"Will the Blend Stay Stable","lesson_keys":["l01-saturates-against-aromatics-and-resins","l02-three-bands-and-three-answers","l03-sara-blends-on-mass","l04-a-rule-of-thumb-can-raise-a-flag","l05-no-gravity-no-screen"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-obigbo-blend-end-to-end","l02-the-obigbo-library-crude-by-crude","l03-what-the-next-tier-changes"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
